          text: 'Every mechanism so far (SN1, SN2, E1, E2, electrophilic addition) has been **polar**: a bond broke with both electrons going to one atom, or an electron pair attacked an electron-poor atom. A bond can also break **evenly**, one electron to each atom. The fragments carry an unpaired electron each: they are [[gchem-free-radical|radicals]], and a whole family of reactions runs on them.',
